      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The chair is considering exempting vehicles there for now.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "3:05:07",
        "endTs": "3:05:37",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The chair said Molokaʻi Community Plan changes would come after the last patient, going to the council and the Molokaʻi Planning Commission.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "3:01:41",
        "endTs": "3:02:38",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "A resource person said a past Department of Hawaiian Home Lands (DHHL) beneficiary working group agreed homesteading would not be part of Kalaupapa.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "2:37:14",
        "endTs": "2:38:06",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The chair said the state asked Maui County to step in because no local government would remain.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "2:09:45",
        "endTs": "2:10:20",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "A committee member asked staff to send the managing director a written question on the county's preparation for the transition.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "1:56:40",
        "endTs": "1:57:10",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "Close public testimony: No one objected, so oral public testimony was closed.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "1:44:51",
        "endTs": "1:45:21",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The state's aquatic resources division plans to write place-based rules for the peninsula but has not started.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:53:18",
        "endTs": "0:53:48",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "He said special peninsula fishing rules will end after the transition; statewide rules will still apply.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:52:46",
        "endTs": "0:53:16",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "Department of Hawaiian Home Lands (DHHL) expects the first of three beneficiary consultation meetings in February or March 2027.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:44:11",
        "endTs": "0:44:45",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "Designate the introduced individuals as resource persons under Rule 18A: No one objected, so the invited speakers were named resource persons (people who can answer the committee's questions).",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:10:03",
        "endTs": "0:10:33",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The chair formed a community advisory group, or hui, which has met three times.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:07:46",
        "endTs": "0:08:47",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The law starts after the last patient leaves; one year later, Maui County takes over the area.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:04:48",
        "endTs": "0:05:27",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-16T18:25:36.541Z"
      },
      "body": "County Council Kōmike Aloha ʻĀina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "The chair said Senate Bill 1432 became Act 171 on June 26, 2026.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "pXD4AJPMtzM",
        "ts": "0:04:42",
        "endTs": "0:05:12",
